<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wexford</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wexford is a port town in south-eastern Ireland at the mouth of the River Slaney. It grew from a Norse settlement of the 9th or 10th century, and in 1169 it became the first town in Ireland captured by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-normans">Anglo-Normans</a>, who had been invited by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diarmait-mac-murchada">Diarmait Mac Murchada</a>, King of Leinster. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oliver-cromwell">Oliver Cromwell</a>'s army stormed and sacked it in 1649.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wexford.jpg" alt="Wexford" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 瑞丽江的河水 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wexford_-_aerial_-_2024-08-31_04.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
